    "readout_text": "To solve the problem, we are given the identity:\n\n$$\n\\tan(2023x) = \\frac{a_1 \\tan x + a_3 \\tan^3 x + a_5 \\tan^5 x + \\cdots + a_{2023} \\tan^{2023} x}{1 + a_2 \\tan^2 x + a_4 \\tan^4 x + \\cdots + a_{2022} \\tan^{2022} x}\n$$\n\nOur goal is to find the value of $ a_{2023} $, which is the coefficient of $ \\tan^{2023} x $ in the numerator of this expression.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Recognize the Structure of the Tangent Multiple-Angle Identity\n\nWe recall the general identity for $ \\tan(nx) $, which can be written as a rational function of $ \\tan x $:\n\n$$\n\\tan(nx) = \\frac{\\sum_{k=0}^{\\lfloor (n-1)/2 \\rfloor} (-1)^k \\binom{n}{2k+1} \\tan^{2k+1} x}{\\sum_{k=0}^{\\lfloor n/2 \\rfloor} (-1)^k \\binom{n}{2k} \\tan^{2k} x}\n$$\n\nThis formula is well-known and can be derived using the binomial expansion of $ (1 + i \\tan x)^n $ and extracting the imaginary and real parts.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Apply the Identity to $ \\tan(2023x) $\n\nSince $ n = 2023 $, the numerator becomes:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{k=0}^{1011} (-1)^k \\binom{2023}{2k+1} \\tan^{2k+1} x\n$$\n\nThis is because the largest odd power of $ \\tan x $ in the numerator is $ \\tan^{2023} x $, which corresponds to $ k = 1011 $ since $ 2k+1 = 2023 \\Rightarrow k = 1011 $.\n\nTherefore, the coefficient $ a_{2023} $ is:\n\n$$\na_{2023} = (-1)^{1011} \\binom{2023}{2023}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Simplify the Expression\n\nWe know that:\n\n- $ \\binom{2023}{2023} = 1 $\n- $ (-1)^{1011} = -1 $, since 1011 is odd\n\nHence,\n\n$$\na_{2023} = -1\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n$$\n\\boxed{-1}\n$$\n\n\\confidence{Almost certain}",
